Inspiration
----------
The design of this tool — an MCP server that inspects binaries, JavaScript
applications and Chromium-family trees without executing them, and returns
answers with their evidence and their limits — follows the work published in
the REA project:

    REA: Reverse Engineer Anything
    https://github.com/morluto/rea
    Licensed under the MIT License
    Copyright (c) 2025 ShuaixinHuang and contributors

No source code from REA was copied into Raqib. The parsers, the evidence
model, the MCP surface, the command line and the console were written from
the public format specifications (System V ELF, the Microsoft PE/COFF
specification, the Electron ASAR format) and from the observed behaviour of
the tools Raqib replaces.

The Chromium-family analysis is designed against the layout of the Chromium
and brave-core source trees:

    brave-core — a fork of Chromium
    https://github.com/brave/brave-core
    Licensed under the Mozilla Public License 2.0
    Copyright (c) 2015–2026 Brave Software, Inc. and Chromium contributors

    Chromium
    https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src
    Licensed under the BSD 3-Clause License
    Copyright (c) 2008–2026 The Chromium Authors

Raqib ships no Chromium or Brave code. It reads trees that belong to their
owners.

